From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ysfaculty <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:02:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 186/194] hjviewer: review fixes for the stray 1 before Korean
 after deleting
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The previous patch dropped filler characters before Hangul on any field
with no typed text. That also dropped 1s the user typed: on a field that
holds a typed 1 (longer than the filler), "1월" arriving in one settled
edit (the iPad keyboard's Paste, a three-finger paste, dictation, text
replacement, or two quick keys on an iPad) reached the PC as "월", where
1.9.3 sent "1월". Its commit message counted only typing, where a 1 and
Hangul never come in one edit because the iPhone keyboard needs a layout
switch between them.

iosSoftKeyboardEdit (flutter/lib/models/soft_keyboard_input.dart) now
drops them only in two shapes: a full filler (as in 1.9.3, any number put
back) and a filler that Backspaces shortened with exactly one character
put back (the device report). A field longer than the filler, and two or
more characters put back on a shortened filler, keep the 1.9.3 behaviour:
the 1s are sent.

Left alone: on a shortened filler with no typed text, "1층" in one edit
(paste or dictation right after deleting text that was on the PC's line)
still arrives as "층"; the field cannot tell it from the keyboard's restored
character. The same drop happened on a full filler in 1.9.3.

Tests: one put back on a shortened filler is dropped, two are sent again
('11한'); a typed 1, then "1월" in one edit, reaches the PC as "11월".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 flutter/lib/models/soft_keyboard_input.dart | 18 +++++++++++-------
 flutter/test/soft_keyboard_input_test.dart  | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 27 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/flutter/lib/models/soft_keyboard_input.dart b/flutter/lib/models/soft_keyboard_input.dart
index f211892..e3abeb2 100644
--- a/flutter/lib/models/soft_keyboard_input.dart
+++ b/flutter/lib/models/soft_keyboard_input.dart
@@ -45,18 +45,22 @@ SoftKeyboardEdit? iosSoftKeyboardEdit(String oldValue, TextEditingValue value,
     return null;
   }
   // The keyboard can also put back one filler character too many before a
-  // syllable (rustdesk PR #15201, "over-restored sentinel"). Also on a filler
-  // that Backspaces shortened: on a device (1.9.3) Korean typed after
-  // deleting text already on the PC's line arrived as "1" and the syllable.
-  // Only while the field holds no typed text and only right before Hangul:
-  // a 1 typed alone, or after typed text, is sent, and typing a 1 and then
-  // Hangul means switching layouts, never one settled edit.
+  // syllable (rustdesk PR #15201, "over-restored sentinel"). Only while the
+  // field holds no typed text and only right before Hangul. On a full filler
+  // any number of them (as in 1.9.3). On a filler that Backspaces shortened
+  // exactly one: on a device (1.9.3) Korean typed after deleting text already
+  // on the PC's line arrived as "1" and the syllable. A field longer than the
+  // filler holds typed 1s, and there a 1 that comes with Hangul in one
+  // settled edit (paste, dictation) is sent.
   if (initialFillerLength != null &&
       !value.isComposingRangeValid &&
       oldFiller == oldValue.length) {
     final newFiller = _fillerLength(newValue);
     final tail = newValue.substring(newFiller);
-    if (newFiller > oldFiller && isHangulText(tail)) {
+    final restored = oldFiller == initialFillerLength
+        ? newFiller > oldFiller
+        : oldFiller < initialFillerLength && newFiller == oldFiller + 1;
+    if (restored && isHangulText(tail)) {
       return (backspaces: 0, text: tail);
     }
   }
diff --git a/flutter/test/soft_keyboard_input_test.dart b/flutter/test/soft_keyboard_input_test.dart
index 2d5dfc0..1a0419b 100644
--- a/flutter/test/soft_keyboard_input_test.dart
+++ b/flutter/test/soft_keyboard_input_test.dart
@@ -107,12 +107,26 @@ void main() {
           iosSoftKeyboardEdit(filler, value('1한', composingFrom: 1),
               initialFillerLength: filler.length),
           (backspaces: 0, text: '1한'));
-      // Also on a filler that Backspaces shortened, also two put back.
+      // On a filler that Backspaces shortened one put back, not two.
       final short = filler.substring(1);
       expect(
-          iosSoftKeyboardEdit(short, TextEditingValue(text: '${short}11한'),
+          iosSoftKeyboardEdit(short, TextEditingValue(text: '${short}1한'),
               initialFillerLength: filler.length),
           (backspaces: 0, text: '한'));
+      expect(
+          iosSoftKeyboardEdit(short, TextEditingValue(text: '${short}11한'),
+              initialFillerLength: filler.length),
+          (backspaces: 0, text: '11한'));
+    });
+
+    test('a typed 1 and Hangul in one edit keep the 1 after typed 1s', () {
+      // Paste, dictation or a quick iPad key: "1월" in one settled edit on a
+      // field that already holds a typed 1 (longer than the filler).
+      final remote = _Remote(filler, shipped)
+        ..apply(TextEditingValue(text: '${filler}1'));
+      expect(remote.text, '1');
+      remote.apply(TextEditingValue(text: '${filler}11월'));
+      expect(remote.text, '11월');
     });
 
     test('Korean after deleting text that was on the PC has no stray 1', () {
